Phase 1 Home Lab Plan (Months 1–3)
Project overview

In Phase 1, I built a Windows-based Active Directory home lab to simulate real IT Support and Service Desk scenarios.
The goal of this lab was to gain hands-on experience with domain administration, user management, Group Policy, DNS, DHCP, and troubleshooting common Windows issues in a controlled environment.

The lab consists of two virtual machines:
VM1 is a Windows Server machine acting as a Domain Controller.
VM2 is a Windows 10 or Windows 11 client joined to the domain.
This lab was built using VirtualBox and evaluation versions of Windows.

